flowchart TB
    N1["1. Technical objective: Guest-facing adapter that exposes shared NeoVM execution APIs in zkVM-compatible form."]
    N2["2. Determinism: same script, stack, gas, and syscall responses produce the same halt/fault state"]
    N3["3. Input constraints: guest bytecode | stack input | shared VM crate"]
    N4["4. Transition rule: opcode semantics, stack rules, gas, and syscall contracts define transitions"]
    N5["5. Verifiable output: guest execution result | public output seed | fault reason"]
    N6["6. Minimal trust: trust canonical NeoVM semantics, not script authors"]
    N7["7. Layer separation: VM semantics stay separate from host context and chain policy"]
    N8["8. Observable evidence: opcode progress, gas, stack digest, fault reason, and syscall boundary"]
    N1 --> N2
    N1 --> N3
    N1 --> N4
    N1 --> N5
    N1 --> N6
    N1 --> N7
    N1 --> N8
    N2 -. constrains .-> N4
    N4 -. produces .-> N5
    N5 -. consumed by .-> N6
